84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 382 0 R
/E (Rolling-bearing defects produce a short impact each time a rolling element passes the damage. These impacts are weak but excite structural resonances at kilohertz frequencies, and they repeat at characteristic defect frequencies set by the bearing geometry.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
85 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 64 0 R
/E (Because bearing impacts are weak and buried under rotor vibration, the standard detection method is envelope analysis [10]. The signal is band-pass filtered around a resonance the impacts excite, its envelope is extracted, and the envelope's spectrum reveals the impact repetition rate. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
