/Title (The four-feature configuration retained the four baseline features with the largest weaker-effect magnitudes: Z band RMS \(4.08\), the envelope feature \(3.30\), Z band power fraction \(2.58\), and Y velocity power fraction \(2.32\). All increased in both comparison groups. Together, they describe high-frequency vibration magnitude, its spectral distribution, envelope modulation and low-frequency velocity redistribution. This provides a rationale for retaining H2 and H5 alongside the envelope feature.)
